## Traps every task hits

- `npm run test:one` writes a shared bundle; run single-file suites
  sequentially to avoid executing the wrong suite.

- `JSON.parse` syntax errors can quote the input. Credential-file parse
  errors must use value-free messages so diagnostic output cannot expose
  a stored key.
- Shell hooks block Bash commands that contain a heredoc mentioning
  `process.env.PATH`, a heredoc or command containing `env:` or `.env`
  text, or a `credentials*` path together with `cat`, `sed`, `head`, and
  the like. Read and write such files with the editor tools.
- Review record initialization follows scope and prompt validation; early
  failures can leave no record, while later failures can retain evidence.
- Tests that write project state (run records, trust, stored
  credentials) chdir into a temporary Git repository first. `.roast/`
  ignores itself, so a leak into this checkout is invisible to
  `git status`; check with `ls -a`.
- CLI diagnostic tests that resolve roles need valid test credentials
  and local fake-server routing, even when asserting only local checks.
  Doctor fakes must route GET models checks and POST inference separately;
  a successful chat probe needs a lookup call followed by a final call
  that echoes the token from the replayed tool result.
- The CLI parser preserves dashed option names and disables boolean
  negation. Declare flags such as `no-browser` explicitly and read
  `args['no-browser']`, rather than a camel-case property.
- `init` login-offer tests that use `simulateTerminals(t, true)` must
  pass `--finder-model` and `--verifier-model` flags, otherwise
  interactive prompts consume stdin before the login offers see it.
- `simulateTerminals` only bypasses interactive-terminal detection. To
  exercise raw-mode prompt input through the CLI, give stdin an `isTTY`
  value of `true` and a `setRawMode` function; assert raw mode is restored.
- Browser-login tests send callbacks with the real fetch; the injected
  provider fetch rewrites every origin. Bound callback tests with
  `loginTimeouts.browser` and set injected display variables on Linux.
- After editing the bundled Roast skill, run `npm run test:one --
  test/skill/assets.ts` to check that bundled bytes match the source.
- Starter comments and runtime config/gate settings share defaults in
  `src/config/defaults.ts`. Review flag defaults should use that module
  too, so starter guidance stays aligned with runtime behavior.
- Login orchestration shares `ctx.lines` across providers and prompts.
  Reuse `providersNeedingLogin` and `loginProvider` for login offers;
  `loginPath` owns the scope rules shared by login and logout.

## Docs

- User-facing docs (`README.md`, `docs/`, the bundled
  `src/skill/assets/roast/SKILL.md`) write every invocation as
  `npx roast ...`; Roast is a project dependency, never a `PATH` binary.
  Settings are documented as `.roast.jsonc` keys, never environment
  variables; only credentials, `ROAST_SKIP`, and test-only `ROAST_LIVE_*`
  / `ROAST_TEST_*` variables exist.
- CLI messages in `src/cli/` (for example the gate hint printed
  during review) still say bare `roast`; changing them is a code change,
  not a docs change.
- Run records can retain arbitrary sensitive content. Metadata excludes
  resolved authentication material and response capture omits HTTP headers,
  but neither is comprehensive redaction of artifact content.
# Roast

An adversarial, cross-model code reviewer installed as a project dependency
via npm. One model proposes defects in a Git diff and a second model checks
surviving candidates when verification runs.

## Language

### Review

**Finder**:
The role whose model reads the diff and proposes candidate findings.
_Avoid_: reviewer, author model

**Verifier**:
The role whose model checks candidate findings against the cited code. It
can confirm, refute, or report insufficient context for a finding.
_Avoid_: checker, judge

**Role**:
One of the two review positions, finder or verifier, each bound to one
inference profile.

**Inference profile**:
A named, complete unit of model, endpoint, protocol, output limit and
credential source.
_Avoid_: provider, backend

**Run record**:
The stored evidence of one review, kept inside the project that was reviewed.
It can contain sensitive reviewed content, prompts, arguments, and provider
responses; excluding resolved authentication material from dedicated metadata
does not make the recorded content credential-free.
_Avoid_: log, history

**Gate**:
The pre-commit hook that runs a quick review of staged content and fails open.
_Avoid_: pre-commit check, hook

### Configuration

**Project config**:
The `.roast.jsonc` file (JSONC) nearest the working directory, searched upward
no further than the Git toplevel. It is the single home for every non-secret
setting.
_Avoid_: repo config, local config, rc file

**Trusted project config**:
A project config whose security-relevant contents (non-default endpoints,
credential variable names, prompt-override files) the user has explicitly
approved for this clone. Roast does not send code or credentials anywhere a
project config names until it is trusted.
_Avoid_: allowed config, whitelisted config

**Credential**:
An API key. Credentials are the only settings that come from outside the
project config: from environment variables, or from a stored credential. A
project config may name the variable but never hold the value.
_Avoid_: secret, token

**Built-in provider**:
A provider Roast knows by name (OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter): its
endpoint, the protocols it accepts there, its standard key variable, and
how to log in.
A selected profile on a built-in provider's endpoint with an accepted
protocol and its standard or implicit key variable requires no approval on
its own; other selected profiles and prompt overrides also matter.
_Avoid_: default provider, known provider

**Stored credential**:
A built-in provider's key kept in a credentials file, scoped to the project
(inside the Git directory) or to the user. It ranks below every environment
variable and is sent only to that provider's own endpoint (ADR-0002).
_Avoid_: saved key, cached token
